## Why This Is Asked
Streaming data often requires maintaining a running statistic under insertions and deletions. The median is robust and a common interview target for dynamic data structures.

## Key Concepts
- Two-heap approach: keep lower half in a max-heap and upper half in a min-heap.
- Duplicates supported; lazy deletion via a delay map.
- Rebalancing invariant: size difference at most 1; median derived from heap tops.

## Code Example
```javascript
class MedianDS {
  constructor(){
    this.lo = new MaxHeap(); // lower half
    this.hi = new MinHeap(); // upper half
    this.delayed = new Map();
    this.sizeLo = 0;
    this.sizeHi = 0;
  }
  _cleanTop(h) {
    const top = h.peek();
    while (top !== null && this.delayed.get(top) > 0) {
      h.pop();
      this.delayed.set(top, this.delayed.get(top) - 1);
    }
  }
  add(x){
    if (this.sizeLo === 0 || x <= this.lo.peek()) {
      this.lo.push(x); this.sizeLo++;
    } else { this.hi.push(x); this.sizeHi++; }
    this._balance();
  }
  remove(x){
    const loTop = this.lo.peek();
    if (loTop !== null && x <= loTop) {
      this.delayed.set(x, (this.delayed.get(x) || 0) + 1);
      this.sizeLo--;
      if (x === loTop) this._cleanTop(this.lo);
    } else {
      this.delayed.set(x, (this.delayed.get(x) || 0) + 1);
      this.sizeHi--;
      this._cleanTop(this.hi);
    }
    this._balance();
  }
  _balance(){
    if (this.sizeLo > this.sizeHi + 1) {
      this.hi.push(this.lo.pop()); this.sizeLo--; this.sizeHi++;
    } else if (this.sizeHi > this.sizeLo) {
      this.lo.push(this.hi.pop()); this.sizeHi--; this.sizeLo++;
    }
    this._cleanTop(this.lo); this._cleanTop(this.hi);
  }
  getMedian(){
    if (this.sizeLo === 0) return null;
    if (this.sizeLo > this.sizeHi) return this.lo.peek();
    return (this.lo.peek() + this.hi.peek()) / 2;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Explores a practical, prefix-based data structure with duplicates, common in autocomplete and search features.

## Key Concepts

- Trie with per-node prefixCount and endCount
- Duplicate tracking via endCount
- Prefix-based queries in O(length(prefix))

## Code Example

```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.next = new Map();
    this.prefixCount = 0;
    this.endCount = 0;
  }
}
class Trie {
  constructor() { this.root = new TrieNode(); }
  insert(word) { let node = this.root; for (const ch of word) { if (!node.next.has(ch)) node.next.set(ch, new TrieNode()); node = node.next.get(ch); node.prefixCount++; } node.endCount++; }
  erase(word) { if (!this.exists(word)) return false; let node = this.root; for (const ch of word) { node = node.next.get(ch); node.prefixCount--; } node.endCount--; return true; }
  countWithPrefix(prefix) { let node = this.root; for (const ch of prefix) { if (!node.next.has(ch)) return 0; node = node.next.get(ch); } return node.prefixCount; }
  exists(word) { let node = this.root; for (const ch of word) { if (!node.next.has(ch)) return false; node = node.next.get(ch); } return node.endCount > 0; }
}
```

